==Strategy==
The general strategy is to stall to max money at the start and then use that money to slowly circlebeat Cumulus and Rangmaster to death.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier is an absolute necessity for dealing with the whole level. Due to his Pseudo-Rusher speed, high stats, and Behemoth Slayer ability, Courier will likely act as the main source of chip damage you have on the boss & Rangmaster. Also helps with the peons.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Jelly Dumpling is an absolute necessity to clear the centillion alien peons that start spawning after base hit. They have a surprising amount of health and dps, which can easily cripple you if you don't kill them.
*[[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]]: Barrel can survive the onslaught of enemies long enough to usually get 1-2 shots off, which combined with its high shield piercing rate can quickly and semi-reliably clear Rangmaster's shield. Pretty necessary because Rangmaster effectively has 2,500,000 health without it.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can sports the Double Money talent, which combined with its high damage can quickly get you money off the starting Wild Doges early game. It can also deal damage to the bosses, albeit inconsistently.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Cyberpunk has the range necessary to outrange nearly everything here, and the constant slow effects are a good source of crowd control and can even swing the entire battle in your favour. Beware that Angaburu can sometimes snipe Cyberpunk with its mini-surge, so don't expect Cyber to stick around long.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Awakened Bahamut, especially with talents, can dish out a ton of damage to the boss very very quickly. Its Explosion talent also means that it will hit every boss instead of just the first one, and it can usually survive 1-3 hits depending on what's hitting it to rebound and deal more damage.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]]: If you have him, basically nullifies Rangmaster as a threat, in tandem with Barrel. Its Behemoth Slayer and 3 knockbacks allows a quite lenient meatshield flow, too. Just protect him from the Alien horde and Rangmaster is as good as dead.

